			<div class="content" id="post-content-4826436">
									

<p>The difference, to me, is a requirement versus a consequence. A cognitohazard could spread and we could harvest a tremendous amount of information about what happens as a result, and then &quot;be ignorant&quot; of the cognitohazard while keeping the adjacent information.</p>
<p>In the scenario I've constructed, containment requires rejecting that sort of information.</p>

